/*Q4. Design a Java class named Car to represent individual cars in a Car Rental System. The class must store the car model and manufacturing
year and provide methods to access and modify these attributes.
Class: Car
The Car class should include the following attributes:
• model (String): Represents the model of the car (for example, Camry or Accord).
• year (int): Represents the manufacturing year of the car.
Implement the following constructors:
• Car(): Initializes a Car object using the default constructor.
• Car(String model, int year): Initializes a Car object with the specified model and manufacturing year.
Implement the following methods:
• getModel(): returns the car model as a String.
• getYear(): returns the manufacturing year as an int.
• setModel(String model): Updates the model of the car.
• setYear(int year): Updates the manufacturing year of the car.
Within the Car class, perform the following operations:
1. Read the car model and manufacturing year.
2. Create an object named rentalCar using the default constructor.
3. Use the setter methods to assign the entered values.
4. Use the getter methods to retrieve and display the car details.
Input Format:
• The first line contains a string representing the car model.
• The second line contains an integer representing the manufacturing year.
Output Format:
Display the car details in the following format:
Model: <car_model>
Year: <car_manufacturing year>
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class Car {
    private String model;
    private int year;
 
    Car() { }
 
    Car(String model, int year) {
        this.model = model;
        this.year = year;
    }
 
    String getModel() { return model; }
    int getYear() { return year; }
    void setModel(String model) { this.model = model; }
    void setYear(int year) { this.year = year; }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String model = sc.nextLine();
        int year = sc.nextInt();
        Car rentalCar = new Car();
        rentalCar.setModel(model);
        rentalCar.setYear(year);
        System.out.println("Model: " + rentalCar.getModel());
        System.out.println("Year: " + rentalCar.getYear());
        sc.close();
    }
}
